  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "JJ has an integer KKK. JJ also has an array AAA of length NNN where (0≤Ai&lt;2K)(0 \\le A_i \\lt 2^K)(0≤Ai​&lt;2K). He can perform the following operations on AAA any number of times (possibly zero):\n\n\nSelect iii and xxx such that 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N and 0≤x&lt;2K0 \\le x \\lt 2^K0≤x&lt;2K and for each 1≤j≤i1 \\le j \\le i1≤j≤i, set Aj:=Aj&amp;xA_j := A_j \\And xAj​:=Aj​&amp;x.\nSelect iii and xxx such that 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N and 0≤x&lt;2K0 \\le x \\lt 2^K0≤x&lt;2K and for each i≤j≤Ni \\le j \\le Ni≤j≤N, set Aj:=Aj∣xA_j := A_j \\mid xAj​:=Aj​∣x.\nHere, &amp;\\And&amp; denotes the bitwise AND operation and ∣\\mid∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation.\n\nDetermine the number of different arrays JJ can obtain by applying the above operations zero or more times. Since the answer can be large, output the answer modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\nTwo arrays PPP and QQQ are said to be different if there exists any index iii such that Pi≠QiP_i \\neq Q_iPi​=Qi​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the size of the array AAA and the parameter KKK mentioned in the statement.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of different arrays JJ can obtain, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤K≤301 \\le K \\le 301≤K≤30",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2K0 \\le A_i \\lt 2^K0≤Ai​&lt;2K",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
